                score -= (m.base.flexibility * (1 - weights.flexibility)); // Penalty for lacking flex if needed

                // Complexity Weight Impact (Reverse: High complexity model is "Harder" if env is simple, "Better" if env is complex)
                // Let's assume Complexity slider = Project Complexity.
                // Simple project (0) + Complex Model (Spiral) = BAD (Low Score)
                // Complex project (100) + Complex Model (Spiral) = GOOD (High Score)
                const complexityDiff = 100 - Math.abs(weights.complexity * 100 - m.base.scalability);
                score += complexityDiff;

                // Team Size Weight Impact
                const teamScore = (weights.teamSize > 0.6) ? m.base.scalability : (100 - m.base.scalability);
                score += (teamScore * 0.2);

                // Normalize roughly to 0-100 for chart visual
                return Math.min(100, Math.max(0, Math.round(score / 2)));

